{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794260844714098002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"nickel-ferric-llama","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"dc3fd3204dc5034aef9bc82b7804cebb0d56adbbb63b04293581cdca1b779956","event_uuid":"9b11b159-3323-4010-810a-7df4c3e9c2b9","position":{"commit_sha":"984e89ce0fbdf23d6006a30d1a627f54d67d6d5c","position":"1794255865742777001-9b11b159-3323-4010-810a-7df4c3e9c2b9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"3606c1f41c4fca8fad7d8ebb4a92231443c4e033ecfbd60a293aff6d9dc6e543","event_uuid":"b10b9c74-e46b-4bdd-8efb-e4701bdc1e8e","position":{"commit_sha":"4502f8034b51413778da4e2a813f65073fc57451","position":"1794256153987481001-b10b9c74-e46b-4bdd-8efb-e4701bdc1e8e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"c7c68bfb56afd1227427fed530f46823b87a324aca7728347908e71d6e4edfb7","event_uuid":"c21681b5-013c-42c6-b769-f9f6ac77ad3e","position":{"commit_sha":"fb4ba61baa275fbbf057dfdb02fb3607c125bc6a","position":"1794256183072514001-c21681b5-013c-42c6-b769-f9f6ac77ad3e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"686747aa70478ea815a12acb0b48bd6b647fcbadc6e09d42f22921351ba16874","event_uuid":"69718760-1924-4750-bb54-a446f154162d","position":{"commit_sha":"9a9ef72fae300594ab68c54bcaa0ad696081f72b","position":"1794257472094517001-69718760-1924-4750-bb54-a446f154162d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"8142dbe74fd71b437643fc04e17f5707b438be3cbe4e9d1e1b0a609a7c744f67","event_uuid":"dc94de65-a2b2-4b2a-865b-25f84142c6a5","position":{"commit_sha":"bb52d71937a87be28354a806a62e1218de64dd2d","position":"1794260844714098001-dc94de65-a2b2-4b2a-865b-25f84142c6a5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794255865742777001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b10b9c74-e46b-4bdd-8efb-e4701bdc1e8e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2886-3079-9b31-4838"},{"link_uuid":"c21681b5-013c-42c6-b769-f9f6ac77ad3e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe parent epic's second engine is a single Opus 5.5 agent that reviews a plan against the code it will touch and reports findings, as an alternative to the 4-pass pipeline. Its starting prompt is the operator's raw review prompt (`~/plan-review-bakeoff/harness/RAWO5_PROMPT.md`), which asks for a JSON array of findings with `id`, `title`, `description`, `severity` (`blocker | major | minor | trivial`), `evidence` and `suggested_fix`, and forbids writing the tree. rebar takes no dependency on that repository: the text is copied into rebar's prompt registry and adapted.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd the engine as its own module, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py`, beside `orchestrator.py` and not inside any near-cap module (the epic's size constraint). It makes ONE call on rebar's existing runner: `RunRequest` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:58`) with `execution_mode=\"agentic\"`, `mode=\"structured\"`, a new packaged output schema for the finding array, and the frontier model class, so the Bedrock-first provider chain, its Anthropic fallback, tracing and usage logging apply unchanged. Budget and timeout use existing `RunRequest` fields only, at the values ADR 0123 adopts: `tool_step_limit=60`, `iteration_limit=80`, model-maximum output tokens, per-request timeout `cfg.timeout_s`; effort comes from the per-model table the model-upgrade ticket adds [rebar:beaten-natural-grouse].\n\nTools are exactly the runner's agentic surface (`runner.py:380-390`): `filesystem_tools` (`read_file`, `list_directory`, `search_files`), `grounding_tools`, and `rebar_tools` with `comment_ticket` withheld. The call runs inside the same gate session as the pipeline, so `assert_gated` (`runner.py:362-369`) holds and `cfg.repo_path` is the attested snapshot of the reviewed ref; `_safe_path` (`src/rebar/llm/fs_tools.py:24`) refuses traversal. No write or execute tool exists on that surface, which is how \"cannot write the checkout or run commands\" is enforced, and a test pins the tool-name set.\n\nThe prompt goes into the packaged registry as `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md` (the directory `prompts.py:119` serves). Adaptations: `@@PLAN_DOC@@` becomes the plan material rebar already assembles for the pipeline (`context_assembly.assemble_context`, including prerequisite blocks), `@@REVIEW_ROOT@@` becomes \"the repository your file tools read\", the \"write to `@@DEST@@`\" instruction becomes \"return the findings as your structured output\", the review criteria context is appended from the same registry `rebar explain <criterion>` renders, each finding gains a `criteria` list of registry criterion ids, possibly empty, matching the pipeline's finding shape, and the bakeoff's scoring language is replaced by the epic's severity rule (only `blocker` blocks). The no-dollar-figures line is kept.\n\nThe workflow gets an `agentic_review` step in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml` that runs `when` the precheck set `run_llm` AND the engine is `agentic`, replacing the not-yet-available raise the engine-switch ticket left [rebar:skilled-cepevorous-naga]. Turning the agent's findings into the verdict and sidecar is the adapter ticket's job; this ticket returns the validated finding list.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py (new)\n- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md (new prompt)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_agentic_findings.schema.json (new output schema)\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml (`agentic_review` step)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (remove the not-yet-available raise)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: with `FakeRunner` (`runner.py:194`) returning a fixed finding array, the engine returns the validated list and the request carries `execution_mode=\"agentic\"`, the frontier class and the new schema.\n- Read-only: a test builds the agentic tool surface and asserts the tool names are exactly the read-only set, with no `comment_ticket`, no write and no execute tool.\n- Failure/edge: malformed output (schema-invalid or non-JSON) and a runner error each surface as an error the adapter can map to INDETERMINATE, never an empty PASS; an empty array is a valid no-findings result.\n- Zero-call invariant: a floor-blocked ticket under `engine=\"agentic\"` makes zero runner calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py` passes, covering the request shape, the read-only tool set, malformed output and the zero-call floor case.\n- [ ] The prompt is served from the packaged registry and contains no `@@` placeholders and no reference to the bakeoff repository (`git grep -nF plan-review-bakeoff -- src` prints nothing).\n- [ ] `agentic.py` is under the 800-line cap and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py","reason":"new engine module"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md","reason":"new prompt"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_agentic_findings.schema.json","reason":"output schema"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml","reason":"agentic_review step"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"remove not-yet-available raise"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","2886-3079-9b31-4838"],["depends_on","7341-7f22-b13a-442c"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2473-79b7-1048-4a71","ticket_type":"story","title":"Agentic plan-review engine: one read-only Opus 5.5 agent on rebar's runner, prompt in the registry","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9b11b159-3323-4010-810a-7df4c3e9c2b9","b10b9c74-e46b-4bdd-8efb-e4701bdc1e8e","c21681b5-013c-42c6-b769-f9f6ac77ad3e","69718760-1924-4750-bb54-a446f154162d","dc94de65-a2b2-4b2a-865b-25f84142c6a5"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794260844714098002,"uuid":"342c2bb0-d5ce-4e49-be33-e4e5a745a7c3"}